; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; ATOM DEFINITIONS (MULT) -- from DEPT-135 (Priority 1) + edited HSQC + formula
; idx  shift    assignment
;  1   178.80   Cq, sp2, in-ring/conjugated C=O
;  2   166.78   Cq, sp2, carbonyl-region C
;  3   164.96   Cq, sp2, bears CH3 25.52 (2J, strongest HMBC); dC(CH3) 25.5 excludes acetyl/acetoxy
;  4   148.83   Cq, sp2
;  5   148.38   CH, sp2, dH 8.892 singlet, NO COSY partner (isolated CH)
;  6   136.21   CH, sp2, dH 8.653 d 8.3
;  7   122.46   CH, sp2, dH 7.393 d 8.1
;  8   119.28   Cq, sp2
;  9   109.81   Cq, sp2 (upfield -- electron-rich / push-pull position)
; 10    47.65   CH2, sp3, dH 4.613 q 7.2
; 11    25.52   CH3, sp3, dH 2.733 s
; 12    15.43   CH3, sp3, dH 1.534 t 7.2
; 13   (N)      N, 3 connections, 0 H  -- position OPEN
; 14   (N)      N, sp2, 0 H            -- position OPEN (sp2 required by parity: 9 sp2 C is odd)
; 15   (O)      sp2 O, carbonyl oxygen of atom 1
; 16   (O)      sp2 O, carbonyl oxygen of atom 2
; 17   (O)      sp3 O-H, carries the exchangeable H (~14.5 ppm, very broad) -- placement OPEN
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
MULT 1 C 2 0     ; 178.80 Cq
MULT 2 C 2 0     ; 166.78 Cq
MULT 3 C 2 0     ; 164.96 Cq
MULT 4 C 2 0     ; 148.83 Cq
MULT 5 C 2 1     ; 148.38 CH  (H 8.892)
MULT 6 C 2 1     ; 136.21 CH  (H 8.653)
MULT 7 C 2 1     ; 122.46 CH  (H 7.393)
