HMBC 10 5        ; 47.65 <- H 8.892   rel_col 176; DA-mandated. Reciprocal half of the N(Et)-CH= evidence.
; C 47.65 fully isolated (nearest 25.52, 22 ppm); H 8.892 unique singlet.
HMBC (4 5) 10    ; 148.83/148.38 <- H 4.613  rel_col 163.8 / 220.4; DA-mandated other half of the pair.
; GROUPED: the two carbons are unresolved in HMBC F1 (span 0.45 ppm) and BOTH
; peaks are present, so LSD must be free to satisfy this with atom 4 OR atom 5.
HMBC (4 5) 5     ; 148.83/148.38 <- H 8.892  rel_col 301.1 / 80.3; GROUPED for the same F1 reason.
; Note the atom-5 branch is a 1J self-term (H5 sits on C5) and so cannot be
; satisfied at 2-3 bonds; the group therefore resolves to atom 4 without my
; having to assert it. Second-strongest unused correlation in the dataset.
HMBC 3 6         ; 164.96 <- H 8.653  rel_col 276; C isolated (nearest 148.83, 16.1 ppm), H isolated
; doublet. Ties the CH3-bearing sp2 carbon to the ortho CH pair.
HMBC 2 5         ; 166.78 <- H 8.892  rel_col 203; C isolated (nearest 164.96, 1.8 ppm -- see note).
; NOTE: 166.78 and 164.96 are 1.82 ppm apart, i.e. inside the 3.0 ppm uniqueness
